+ * Follow the page.
+ *
+ * Where it shows. PMConcept7 hangs the panorama in a fixed layer behind its whole shell, and its open issue is that the
+ * opaque panels of a dense page hide it. Here the scene IS the transcript stage's own background: the stage reads as
+ * ground with the scene at the foot of it, under the conversation, fading out toward the top (a ground-coloured
+ * gradient, no mask), and the rest of the concept keeps its panels. No layer is added to the page, so the app's DOM
+ * patch never meets one, and the stage scrolls over a background that stays put (a scroll container's own background).
