+ * live. Colours are the palette's helper tokens (nier.css); the line art (empty states, machine glyphs) is the data: SVG
+ * that nier_palette_56.py writes per mode into nier.css's generated block (--o55nw-art-*). No colour literal here.
+ * Motion rules (PMConcept7's): continuous motion is transform or opacity only (the save diamond's turn is the one loop);
+ * a block fill steps instead of gliding; nothing animates a clip-path, filter, mask or background. Everything that moves
+ * stops under the three reduced-motion routes (the media query, html[data-motion="reduced"], body.pm56-reduced).
+ * Overlays never take a click. Selector rules (tests/shell-selfcheck.cjs): no :has(), no rightmost bare :is() list.
+ */
+
+/* ================================================================================ Boot sequence [boot] */
+/* nier-world.js shows #o55nw-boot once, when the concept opens in a NieR theme: a mono log over the boot paint, about a
+   second, then it clears. It never takes a click, and a key or a click clears it at once. */
+#o55nw-boot { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 2147483400; pointer-events: none; contain: strict; overflow: hidden;
+  background: var(--o55-nier-paper); color: var(--o55-nier-ink);
